            "result_text": "Done! The function uses:\n- **`asyncio.Semaphore`**: Limits how many tasks run concurrently\n- **`return_exceptions=True`**: Ensures all tasks run to completion even if one fails, so finally blocks in each task execute\n- **KeyboardInterrupt handling**: When you press Ctrl+C, the event loop will propagate the interrupt, but tasks already running will finish (including their cleanup code in finally blocks)\n\nYou can import and use it like:\n```python\nfrom run import run_tasks\n\nasync def my_task():\n    try:\n        await some_work()\n    finally:\n        # cleanup always runs\n        pass\n\nawait run_tasks([my_task, my_task, my_task], max_concurrent=2)\n```"
